2:T689,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Which is the best AI planner app for Indian students?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For exam-focused students who want the app to build and adjust their daily timetable, PlanBot is the strongest fit - its AI generates day plans around your syllabus, weak subjects, and energy patterns, with INR pricing from free to Rs 249. General organizers like Todoist or TickTick are better if you mainly want task lists."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a completely free AI planner?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Google Calendar is free but does not plan for you - it stores what you enter. PlanBot's free tier generates AI daily plans with limits, and its web tools (schedule generator, revision calculator) are completely free without signup."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much do planner apps cost in India for students?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Global apps bill in USD: Todoist Pro is $5/month billed yearly, Motion starts around $19/month billed yearly - both add up to Rs 500-1,600 a month. Indian-priced apps like PlanBot bill in INR (paid tiers from Rs 99), which matters on a student budget."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do AI planner apps actually work for JEE or NEET preparation?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The good ones do what a static timetable cannot: they rebalance every day around what you actually completed, weight weak subjects heavier, and schedule spaced revision. That daily adaptation is the entire advantage - an app that only stores your tasks adds little over a paper timetable."}}]}a:["slug","best-ai-planner-apps-indian-students-2026","d"]
